1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,518
Slide 38 clarifies "HUMAN-ON-THE-LOOP (HOTL): Strategic Supervision vs.

2
00:00:06,518 --> 00:00:07,840
Micromanagement."

3
00:00:08,740 --> 00:00:16,767
Old Model: Human-IN-the-loop, where the human must approve every single mouse click and keystroke.

4
00:00:16,767 --> 00:00:19,470
Slow, exhausting, and unscalable.

5
00:00:20,370 --> 00:00:30,790
New Model: Human-ON-the-loop, where agents execute autonomously within predefined guardrails, and the human observes telemetry dashboards and intervenes only on strategic exceptions.

6
00:00:31,690 --> 00:00:36,110
HOTL provides maximum scalability with complete safety.

7
00:00:37,010 --> 00:00:46,370
Instead of reviewing 500 lines of boilerplate code line-by-line, you review high-level architectural invariants, Grafana metric dashboards, and audit summaries.

8
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:55,720
It preserves human agency, prevents decision fatigue, and multiplies operational throughput by orders of magnitude.

